---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import ProjectHeader from "../../components/ProjectHeader.astro";
import "../../styles/projects.css";
import { person } from "../../data/site";
---
<Base title="Projects | David Lindgreen" description="Three connected projects on public financial data: a pharma valuation explorer, an annual-report research assistant and an M&A screening workbench. Honest status for each.">
  <ProjectHeader current="projects" />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="wrap proj-hero">
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p class="proj-lede">Three connected tools built on public financial data. Each has an identifiable user, a decision it supports, traceable inputs and a result that can be evaluated. Their status is stated plainly.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" aria-label="Projects">
      <div class="proj-list">
        <article class="proj-item">
          <div>
            <p class="status">First release · in development</p>
            <h3 style="margin-top:1rem">Pharma Valuation Explorer</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>A like-for-like comparison of Novartis, AstraZeneca and GSK from SEC filings, a DCF of AstraZeneca with sensitivity analysis, and a downloadable model with sources. 137 figures reconciled to filing pages; 168 automated checks pass; not yet independently reviewed.</p>
            <p class="links"><a href="/projects/pharma-valuation/">Open the explorer</a><a href="/projects/pharma-valuation/#evidence">See the evidence</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="proj-item">
          <div>
            <p class="status">First release · in development</p>
            <h3 style="margin-top:1rem">Annual-Report Research Assistant</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>Ask questions across the FY2025 reports of Novartis, AstraZeneca and GSK. Answers are quoted source passages with links into the filing, calculations from the reconciled dataset, or an explicit refusal; there is no language model in this version. Evaluated on 67 hand-written questions in a development set and a held-out set, with failures listed; not yet independently reviewed.</p>
            <p class="links"><a href="/projects/research-assistant/">Open the assistant</a><a href="/projects/research-assistant/#evaluation">See the evaluation</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="proj-item">
          <div>
            <p class="status">First release · in development</p>
            <h3 style="margin-top:1rem">Strategic M&amp;A Screening Workbench</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>An explainable preliminary shortlist for a clearly labelled hypothetical buyer brief, over 28 US-listed pharma and biotech companies from SEC filings. Adjustable criterion weights, missing-data flags, ranking sensitivity and a generated screening memo. It supports initial screening only; it makes no valuation or deal-feasibility claim. Figures checked against the filing text; not independently reviewed.</p>
            <p class="links"><a href="/projects/ma-screening/">Open the workbench</a><a href="/projects/ma-screening/#evidence">See the evidence</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="callout" style="margin-top:1.5rem">Smaller experiments, implementation lessons and evaluation findings live in <a href={person.labNotes} rel="noopener">Lab Notes</a>. Future ideas such as an acquisition economics simulator or a credit-risk monitor are kept on a backlog and are not built as thin extras.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="wrap proj-foot"><p><a href="/">Home</a> · David Lindgreen · Frankfurt, Germany</p></footer>
  </main>
</Base>
